of her own positive feminine qualities of nurturing, relationship building, and
emotional expressiveness to "get ahead."
The separation from the personal mother is a particularly intense process
for a daughter because she has to separate from the one who is most like herself.
She experiences a fear of loss characterized by anxiety about being alone, sep-
arate, and different from the one who in most cases has been her primary rela-

