death; she loses a sibling or child through serious illness, drug
addiction, or an accident. A life-threatening illness or life cir-
cumstance makes her face her own mortality. She finds herself "wandering for
seven years in the forest," undergoing an initiation process of the soul, facing
all the aspects of her wounded, disheveled self that she has projected onto her
arents, spouse, or others.
