She looks at me coldly. Her hooked fish
mouth presses tighter.
The needle stings her blue-blooded alabaster arm.
I scream and sob myself awake.
My lover enfolds me to his heart
and my horror hyperventilates me.
In our boxcar apartment
in the Calle Convento
in Santurce, humid night bathes
me. Coqui. Coqui. Coqui.
